Title: Show canonical and analytical evidence depth in the JETP MVP
Created: 2026-09-16
Author: Codex under author-authorised autonomous orchestration
Blocked-by: 0824

--- log ---
2026-09-16T00:00Z Created after author feedback that the MVP hid recently structured evidence.
--- body ---

## Context

The prepared 2026-11 MVP keeps the analytical snapshot out of the canonical
public edition, correctly. Its "What changed, and what did not" page therefore
makes recent progress invisible: visitors see only three reviewed canonical
records rather than the difference between canonical evidence, frozen document
coverage and analytical staging. Expose those layers without aggregating or
promoting staging data.

## First test

With a fixture containing 3 reviewed canonical records, 301 frozen sources and
1,740 staged atomic observations, render the edition page. It must show each
count with its layer, state that the staged observations are not deployed as
canonical facts, and must not present their sum as one common record total.

## Actions

Add an explicit evidence-depth summary to "What changed, and what did not":
canonical reviewed records, frozen source documents and structured analytical
observations, including country coverage where available. Link the staged
snapshot/manifest as a derived local research artifact only if this can be done
without deploying it as a canonical data route. Explain that the 279 Vietnam
RMP positions and other extracted records are structured observations, not
automatically reconciled operations or payments. Preserve offline replay,
release immutability, non-aggregation and snapshot `not_deployed` boundary.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Page exposes canonical, source and analytical counts as separate layers
- [ ] Vietnamese 279-position extraction is visible as staging coverage, not a new canonical portfolio count
- [ ] No analytical amount, reconciliation or estimate is presented as canonical fact
- [ ] Prior archive and current release remain internally reproducible
- [ ] UI tests cover labels, counts and non-aggregation boundary

## Links

Follows 0824. The analytical inputs remain owned by 0822/0730 and are not a
public release promotion.
